 operates through Powered Vehicles Group (PVG), Aftermarket Applications Group (AAG), and Specialty Sports Group (SSG) segments. The company offers powered vehicle products for off-road vehicles and trucks, side-by-sides, on-road vehicles with and without off-road capabilities, all-terrain vehicles, snowmobiles, specialty vehicles and applications, and motorcycles; aftermarket truck suspension components, including two-inch bolt-on shocks and position sensitive internal bypass shocks; and suspension systems, as well as motorcycle shocks, forks, cushioning, and hydraulic components. It also provides lift kits and components with shock products; aftermarket accessory packages for trucks; suspension tuning services; wheels, off-road tires, and accessories; superchargers, interior accessories, tires, lighting, and body enhancements; and mid-end and high-end front fork and rear suspension products. In addition, the company offers mountain and gravel bike wheels; cranks, chainrings, pedals, bars, stems, and seat posts. Further, it provides aftermarket applications products; upfitting products; and mountain bikes, e-bikes, and gravel bikes. The company sells its products to OEMs through dealers, distributors, and direct-to-consumer channels under the FOX, Marzocchi, Race Face, Easton Cycling, BDS Suspension, Zone Offroad, JKS Manufacturing, RT Pro UTV, 4x4 Posi-Lok, Ridetech, Fox Factory Vehicles, Black Widow, Rocky Ridge, Outside Van, Custom Wheel House, Method Race Wheels, Badlander, Black Ops, Harley-Davidson, and Shelby American brands. Fox Factory Holding Corp. was incorporated in 2007 and is based in Duluth, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Douglas J. Grimm | Interim CEO & Director | Age 63","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $397K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $7K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Fox Factory Holding Corp. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $741M market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -4.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $27M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -4.2pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 43% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 30% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2950486491252432},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 31% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to FOXF Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/Technical_Reactions_to_FOXF_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_112126074202_1795264922.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795264922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fox Factory (NASDAQ:FOXF) Stock: Insider Toby Merchant Sells 1,375 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/fox-factory-nasdaqfoxf-stock-insider-toby-merchant-sells-1375-shares.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794776234.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Is Fox Factory (NASDAQ:FOXF) Navigating Changing Demand?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/how-is-fox-factory-nasdaqfoxf-navigating-changing-demand","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794682800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"tit